# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and machine-specific material
#
# The column encryption key, SMTP credentials and connection strings belong in
# environment variables, user-secrets or a key vault - never here. The API
# refuses to start outside Development without a real encryption key, so an
# accidental omission fails loudly instead of quietly using the published
# development value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
appsettings.Production.json
appsettings.Staging.json
appsettings.*.local.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
.env
.env.*
secrets.json

# The development certificate the verification scripts export. It is per
# machine; tools/api-tests/README.md says how to produce it.
tools/api-tests/ensa-dev-cert.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored on purpose. `logs/` and `documents/` without a leading path match a
# directory of that name at EVERY level, and Git on Windows is case-insensitive
# by default - so `documents/` also matched src/Ensa.Domain/Documents/ and five
# other source folders, and none of them were ever committed. An ignored source
# file is a silent failure: the build keeps passing locally and a clone does not
# compile. tools/repo-check/check_tracked_sources.py now fails if it recurs.
/src/Ensa.HttpApi.Host/Logs/
/src/Ensa.HttpApi.Host/App_Data/
/logs/
/documents/
*.log
received_mail.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python helpers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
